{{etymon|en|id=make sound|:inh|enm:speken|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|speke}}, {{m|enm|speken|t=to speak}}, from {{inh|en|ang|specan|t=to speak}}. This is usually taken to be an irregular alteration of earlier {{m|ang|sprecan}}, {{m|ang|spreocan|t=to speak}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*sprekan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sprekaną|t=to speak, make a sound}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*spreg-|t=to make a sound, utter, speak}}. Finding this proposed loss of ''r'' from the stable cluster ''spr'' unparalleled, Hill instead sets up a different root, {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*spekan||to negotiate}} from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*bʰeh₂g-|*bʰégʾ-e-|t=to distribute}} with *''s''-mobile, which collapsed in meaning with *''sprekan'' ("to speak" < "to crackle, prattle") and so came to be seen as a free variant thereof.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|speak}}, {{m|sco|speik|t=to speak}}, {{cog|stq|spreke|t=to speak}}, {{cog|fy|sprekke|t=to speak}}, {{cog|gmw-cfr|sjprèche|t=to speak}}, {{cog|nl,nds|spreken|t=to speak}}, {{cog|de|sprechen|t=to speak}}, {{cog|lb|spriechen|t=to speak}}, and also with {{cog|sq|shpreh|t=to express, manifest, show}} through Indo-European.
{{col-bottom}}

