===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|spoon}}, {{m|enm|spoune}}, {{m|enm|spone}}, {{m|enm|spon|t=spoon, chip of wood}}, from {{inh|en|ang|spōn|t=sliver, chip of wood, shaving}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*spānu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*spēnuz|t=chip, flake, shaving}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)peH-|t=chip, shaving, log, length of wood}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|spun}}, {{m|sco|spon|t=spoon, shingle}}, {{cog|fy|spoen|t=chip}}, {{cog|nl|spaan|t=chip, flinders}}, {{cog|de|Span|t=chip, flake, shaving}}, {{cog|sv|spån|t=chip, flake}}, {{cog|nn|spon||chip, spoon}}, {{cog|fo|spónur|t=wood chip; spoon}}, {{cog|grc|σφήν|t=wedge}}(though the connection to the Greek is likely impossible by modern reconstructions of PIE). Eclipsed non-native {{noncog|enm|cuculer}}, {{m|enm|coclear|t=spoon}}, from {{ncog|ang|cuculer}}, {{m|ang|cuceler}}, {{m|ang|cucler}}, borrowed from {{ncog|la|cochlear|t=spoon}}.

The "metaphoric unit of personal energy" sense was {{coinage|en|Christine Miserandino|w=-|in=2003|occ=writer|occ2=disability advocate|nobycat=1|nocap=1}} (see {{m|en|spoon theory}}).<ref name="Miserandino">{{cite-web|url=https://butyoudontlooksick.com/articles/written-by-christine/the-spoon-theory/|title=The Spoon Theory|last=Miserandino|first=Christine|year=2003|site=But You Don't Look Sick|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20191117210039/https://butyoudontlooksick.com/articles/written-by-christine/the-spoon-theory/|archivedate=17 November 2019|accessdate=12 October 2022}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|scooped utensil}} An implement for eating or serving; a [[scoop]]ed [[utensil]] whose long handle is straight, in contrast to a [[ladle]].
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Comedy of Errors|IV|iii|passage=He must have a long '''spoon''' that must eat with the devil.}}
# An implement for stirring food while being prepared; a [[wooden spoon]].
# A [[measure]] that will fit into a spoon; a [[spoonful]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1978|author=Illinois. Supreme Court|title=Reports of Cases at Law and in Chancery...|page=76
|passage=While Ms. Fly was with Sharon in the kitchen, Sharon asked the defendant for a “'''spoon''' of drugs.” Defendant refused and stated that he did not know where drugs could be obtained.}}
# {{lb|en|golf|archaic}} A wooden-headed [[golf club]] with moderate loft, similar to the modern [[fairway wood]]. <!--Wikipedia self-contradicts, in some places saying it's equiv to a FIVE wood-->
# {{lb|en|slang}} An [[oar]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1877|journal=The Country|volume=1-2|page=339
|passage=To this class college rowing offers no attractions or place, nor are they generally looked upon by the artists of the "'''spoons'''" as a desirable addition {{...}}}}
# {{senseid|en|fishing lure}} {{lb|en|fishing}} A type of metal [[lure]] resembling the [[concave]] head of a [[tablespoon]].
# {{lb|en|dentistry|informal}} A [[spoon excavator]].
# A [[South African]] [[shrub]] of the genus {{taxlink|Spatalla|genus}}.
# {{lb|en|figuratively|slang|archaic}} A [[simpleton]], a [[spoony]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1872|author=w:George Eliot|title=w:Middlemarch|chapter=[[s:Middlemarch (1871)/Chapter 23|Chapter 23]]
|passage=To get all the advantages of being with men of this sort, you must know how to draw your inferences and not be a '''spoon''' who takes things literally.}}
# {{senseid|en|grenade handle}} {{lb|en|US|military}} A safety handle on a [[hand grenade]], a trigger.
# {{sid|en|metaphoric unit of human energy}} {{lb|en|slang}} A [[metaphoric]] [[unit]] of [[finite]] [[physical]] and [[mental]] [[energy]] available for daily activities, especially in the context of living with [[chronic illness]] or [[disability]].
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://spooniesophia.com/2014/03/12/the-spoon-theory-rationing-my-legs-and-energy/|work=Spoonie Sophia|passage=We therefore have to meticulously plan out each day with the small amount of '''spoons''' we have. Each task will cost us at least one '''spoon'''.|title=The Spoon Theory – Rationing my Legs & Energy|date=2014-03-12|publisher=WordPress|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220625170751/http://spooniesophia.com/2014/03/12/the-spoon-theory-rationing-my-legs-and-energy/|archivedate=25 June 2022}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015  |title=Furiously Happy: A Funny Book About Horrible Things|author=Jenny Lawson |page=241|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=FS6NBwAAQBAJ&pg=PA241&dq=%22damn+spoons%22 |ISBN=|passage=You work, and play, and clean, and love, and hate, and that's lots of damn '''spoons''' . . . but if you are young and healthy you still have '''spoons''' left over as you fall asleep and wait for the new supply of '''spoons''' to be delivered in the morning.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016 |title=Two Against Nature |author=Tymber Dalton |page=86 |ISBN=|passage=Once you're out of '''spoons''' for the day, that's it, no more energy. So when you get down to your last couple of '''spoons''' for the day, you have to decide, what's the priority?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018 |title=Adulting 101: Writing Through Life and Other Adventures|author=Donna Alward; Nancy Cassidy |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=EEpBDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT24&dq=%22low+on+spoons%22 |passage=But if you're running low on '''spoons''', take some time out to recharge.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2018|title=Zoe Died. What Now?: Finding Hope in Times of Loss| author=Dennis J. DeWitt|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=OPRhDwAAQBAJ&pg=PT121&dq=%22they+have+run+out+of+spoons.%22| passage=He has frequent dizzy spells. His friend has Asperger syndrome. Both relate and support each other when they have run out of '''spoons'''.}}

