|passage=She'd sit by the fire, arms crossed, demanding that Ruby '''spike''' her tea with a cinder. But Ruby would never give in to her demands, no matter how much her mam begged. There was no alcohol in the house now; Arthur had made sure of that in an effort to get Mary sober.}}
# To add a small amount of one substance to another.
