===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[restore]] to ease, comfort, or [[tranquility]]; relieve; calm; [[quiet]]; [[refresh]].
#: {{syn|en|becalm|placate|Thesaurus:pacify}}
#* {{RQ:Congreve Mourning Bride|page=1|passage=Muſick has Charms to '''ſooth''' a ſavage Breaſt, <br> To ſoften Rocks, or bend a knotted Oak.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=11 October 2013|author=Daniel Taylor|journal=The Guardian|url=http://www.theguardian.com/football/2013/oct/11/england-montenegro-world-cup-qualifier
|passage=Yet Wayne Rooney scored at a good time, three minutes after the restart, to '''soothe''' any gathering nerves and the night can ultimately be chalked off as one of the finest occasions of Hodgson's 17 months in the job.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[allay]]; [[assuage]]; [[mitigate]]; [[soften]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|rare}} To [[smooth]] over; render less obnoxious.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[calm]] or [[placate]] someone or some situation.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[ease]] or [[relieve]] [[pain]] or [[suffering]].
#: {{syn|en|comfort|solace|Thesaurus:comfort}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1976|author=w:The Wurzels|title=I Am A Cider Drinker
|passage=I am a cider drinker, I drinks it all of the day<br>I am a cider drinker, it '''soothes''' all me troubles away}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[temporise]] by assent, concession, flattery, or cajolery.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To bring [[comfort]] or [[relief]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To keep in good humour; [[wheedle]]; [[cajole]]; [[flatter]].
#: {{syn|en|jolly|lay it on thick|puff|Thesaurus:flatter}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[prove]] [[true]]; [[verify]]; [[confirm]] as true.
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To confirm the statements of; [[maintain]] the truthfulness of (a person); [[bear out]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[assent]] to; [[yield]] to; humour by agreement or concession.
#: {{syn|en|comply|give way|Thesaurus:accede}}
#* {{RQ:Plutarch Holland Morals|chapter=Of the Nouriture and Education of Children|page=15|passage=To be ſhort, a wretched and curſed generation they be; hypocrites, pretending friendſhip, but they can not skill of plaine dealing and franke ſpeech. Rich men they claw, '''ſooth''' up and flatter: the poore they contemne and despiſe.}}

